{"version":1,"summary":"Requires Go 1.27.3 so govulncheck no longer reports GO-2026-6809, and stops concurrent test children from racing on one coverage directory.","files":[{"path":"go.mod","summary":"Raises the go directive to 1.27.3.","annotations":[{"newRange":[3,3],"summary":"The go directive moves from 1.27.2 to 1.27.3, the release that fixes GO-2026-6809.","rationale":"Go 1.27.2 ships a vulnerable crypto/x509, so the vuln check is red on main. CI reads go-version-file: go.mod, so this line selects the fixed toolchain. Verified with scripts/ci on Go 1.27.3 and the GitHub vuln check.","author":"fm/verilex-go-1273"}]},{"path":"tests/run_test.go","summary":"Gives each spawned CLI its own GOCOVERDIR subdirectory.","annotations":[{"newRange":[131,139],"summary":"command() points every child at a unique child-N coverage subdirectory under GOCOVERDIR.","rationale":"Six children exiting together wrote the same covmeta temp file name on macOS, so one rename failed and a test saw exit 2. Separate directories remove the shared name. The race itself only shows on macOS CI.","author":"fm/verilex-go-1273"}]},{"path":"scripts/ci","summary":"Gathers child coverage files into the cover root before covdata reads it.","annotations":[{"newRange":[57,60],"summary":"One covmeta and every covcounters file move into the root, then covdata percent reads the root alone.","rationale":"A comma-joined -i list would pass the 128 KiB argument limit under a long TMPDIR, and mv -n exits 1 on duplicate covmeta files with newer GNU coreutils. Moving one covmeta (all are identical) avoids both. Counter names carry pid and time, so none collide. Verified with scripts/ci under a long COVER_OUT path; the plain mv works on BSD and GNU.","author":"fm/verilex-go-1273"}]}]}
